1
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,920
Oh, Yoshikage, my darling
boy, where are you?

2
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:12,042
I've looked all over and
can't find you anywhere.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:16,317
You must have been forced to change
your face and name and go into hiding.

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,518
My heart aches for you, my poor son.

5
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,580
I'll make sure they pay dearly.

6
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:21,820
You got that?

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,537
We need to look further into
the recent missing person cases.

8
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:26,973
That includes runaways.

9
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:30,460
Hang on, didn't Kira go into hiding?

10
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:34,537
You really think he'd risk capture
by continuing his murdering spree?

11
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:37,577
He won't be able to brush
aside his murderous impulses.

12
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,778
That's just how serial killers work.

13
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,580
He will kill again.

14
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:48,957
I wonder if just waiting for something
to happen is the best way to go.

15
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:52,377
And all this time we still haven't
found a single clue leading us to Kira.

16
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:54,717
Well, it's been bothering me a lot, too.

17
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,497
But you guys remember what
Jotaro said, don't you?

18
00:00:57,580 --> 00:01:00,137
As soon as he finds something,
we spring to action.

19
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:03,717
According to him, we should go back
to being ordinary students until then.

20
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,617
I'd rather hunt down that bastard Kira
than go back to hitting the books.

21
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,757
We almost got him before, so I
bet the next time we see him,

22
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,487
it'll be a one-two knockout.

23
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:14,830
Yes,

24
00:01:14,913 --> 00:01:16,617
and since I'm repairing the fire damage,

25
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,697
I'd like to have some
renovations done, too.

26
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,280
That little punk!

27
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:23,557
He's snapping pictures of
people in search of my son!

28
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:26,111
Now, would you mind giving me an estimate?

29
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:30,480
Jotaro and his insufferable stand-user
posse think they're so smart!

30
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,160
I'll annihilate these parasites!

31
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,320
And the best way to do that is
by creating new stand-users!

32
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:38,990
Huh?

33
00:01:39,073 --> 00:01:40,060
Wait a minute!

34
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,980
No doubt about it!

35
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:52,277
Altered appearance or not, the bond
of a father and son can't be broken!

36
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:54,920
I could never mistake my son for another!

37
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,220
I found you at last, Yoshikage!

38
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,920
Just you wait.

39
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:06,400
I'll find out who you
really are, imposter.

40
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:08,677
You have to be kidding me!

41
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:13,580
If that brat uncovers my son's secret,
the stand users will sniff him out.

42
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:15,521
Enough's enough.

43
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,426
I have to put an end to this.

44
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:21,440
I'll protect Yoshikage with
every fiber of my being.

45
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:19,540
Let the voice of love take you higher.

46
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,880
See ya later!

47
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:53,541
I'm going to be late, and
I'm class monitor today.

48
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:05,620
I stayed up way too late. I'm exhausted.

49
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:07,337
Man, that sucks for you.

50
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:10,317
I look like a rock, so I'm
feeling as fit as a fiddle.

51
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,080
Check it out, Josuke! Hmm?

52
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:14,100
Some random binoculars!

53
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,517
Somebody must have left them behind!

54
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:19,297
Wow, it doesn't take much to pique
your interest, does it, buddy?

55
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:20,560
Don't pick them up.

56
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:21,490
That's gross.

57
00:04:21,573 --> 00:04:22,480
What? You think?

58
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:25,180
I can assure you I am not gross.

59
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,440
Hello, Josuke and Okuyasu.

60
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:31,040
Oh, it's you again.

61
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:33,137
Don't scare us like that, Mikitaka.

62
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,050
No kidding.

63
00:04:34,133 --> 00:04:36,377
My heart isn't built
for that kind of shock.

64
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:37,917
Oh, you're being too kind.

65
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,817
That wasn't a compliment, you know.

66
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:41,197
Oh, yeah, that's right.

67
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,809
You've got perfect timing.

68
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:45,717
It's high time for you to come
clean about something, Mr.

69
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:46,630
Alien Man.

70
00:04:46,713 --> 00:04:48,857
You're not actually from
outer space, are you?

71
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:51,757
You're just a run-of-the-mill
stand-user who believes he's

72
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:55,664
an alien for some reason spell
the beans all this lion ain't cool

73
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,240
What do you mean?

74
00:04:57,340 --> 00:05:00,517
I have no beans and I
really am an alien There

75
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,637
you go talking like a
freaking weirdo again,

76
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:07,485
so here's a question for you Why were you
lying out here as a pair of binoculars?

77
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:09,160
It's a little weird Well,

78
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:13,757
I wanted the two of you to see something
hence my waiting here in the open

79
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:14,670
That?

80
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,470
Yes.

81
00:05:17,553 --> 00:05:19,394
It's a transmission tower, to be exact.

82
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:21,020
Huh, you don't say.

83
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:25,857
Eh, calling it that might be a bit of a
stretch, without any of its power lines.

84
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:27,737
It's more of a relic of the past.

85
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,820
When redevelopment took over here,

86
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:33,437
most of the excess power lines were
taken down and moved underground.

87
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,397
Why did you want us to see that old thing?

88
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:38,637
Is that what you're using to
communicate with life on other planets?

89
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:43,177
Unless I'm mistaken, there's smoke wafting
up from around the center of the tower.

90
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,090
Hmm?

91
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,920
Whoa, you're right!

92
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,760
Yeah, how weird.

93
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,780
Please use me to take a closer look.

94
00:05:59,140 --> 00:05:59,970
What the?

95
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,160
There's a kettle! Seriously?

96
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,917
But how is that possible?

97
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,257
That tower is like 20 meters in the air!

98
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:09,760
Indeed, but aim me about
five meters higher. Huh? Huh?

99
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,040
You don't see that every day.

100
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,478
Stop hogging the alien, I wanna see!

101
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,980
Oh wow, it's a dude!

102
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:30,097
There's a guy sitting up
there cooking some grub!

103
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:31,540
What? Let me see.

104
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:35,113
I think that tower might be
his home, and he looks comfy?

105
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:37,577
so he's probably spent
his entire life up there.

106
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,937
He can fish from the river and
he's got cucumbers growing.

107
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,432
Nice, that's impressive.

108
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,400
I have to agree with you.

109
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:48,317
It's like this guy is living in one
of those fancy self-sufficient homes.

110
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,460
This world has no shortages
of curious individuals.

111
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:58,920
Look out!

112
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:11,117
did you see that this guy has to be a
new stand user he just flew right through

113
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:15,517
the air like it was nothing yeah i know
but what's a stand user doing living

114
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:19,877
on a transmission tower if we want to
find out the answer to that i believe

115
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:24,377
we'll need to take a closer look what do

116
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:27,457
you know they've arrived at last i wonder

117
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:32,557
what i did to finally catch their curious
eyes come on over it's been quite a

118
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:37,577
while since i've indulged in a little chit
chat check it out looks like that tower

119
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:42,457
dude might have noticed that we noticed
him you want to get closer oh yeah but

120
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:46,217
we have to play it safe we still don't I
don't know if that user is on our side,

121
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:48,300
or if he's angling to take us out.

122
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:58,297
Is there something I can do for you?

123
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:00,780
Sorry to be rude, but I'm kinda in...

124
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:13,752
This thing looks a lot bigger
once you get up close to it.

125
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:17,037
If you fellas know what's good for you,

126
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,957
you'll stop right there
and won't get any closer.

127
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,537
Didn't you two hear what I said?

128
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,450
Get back!

129
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:24,677
I just answered the call
of nature, and trust me,

130
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:27,466
you don't want to be
there to get the message.

131
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:29,291
I'm really not following.

132
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:31,060
What the hell?

133
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,398
This is disgusting!

134
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:35,177
Don't say I didn't warn you.

135
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:37,201
I needed to fertilize the garden.

136
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:38,601
That's so gross!

137
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,717
Watch your mouth!

138
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:40,657
That's impolite!

139
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:43,257
I designed this nifty
contraption so it would

140
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:46,257
distribute the fertilizer
to all the plants below.

141
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:49,281
I'm all about that zero-waste
lifestyle, you know.

142
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:53,800
On the right are Asiatic dayflowers,
mountain asparagus, and watercress.

143
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:55,705
They're all completely edible!

144
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:58,057
And with all of these plants around,

145
00:08:58,140 --> 00:09:02,846
catching nibbling rabbits is a cinch, so
I've got the best of both worlds, baby!

146
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:06,100
No way, so you're really
living up there all alone?

147
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:09,400
Doesn't this tower belong
to some electric company?

148
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,357
What are you talking about?

149
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,257
I paid for this house with my own money.

150
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:14,170
It's all mine.

151
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:17,577
I bought this abandoned
tower for 100,000 yen and

152
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:20,980
transformed it into my
self-sufficient dream house.

153
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,277
You bought it?

154
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,880
For 100,000 yen?

155
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,577
Yes, that's right.

156
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:26,542
It was a steal.

157
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:30,157
Since I support myself, I'm not
stuck working for some lame company.

158
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,197
It's a pretty sweet life
if you think about it.

159
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:36,277
I don't have to leave the house, and I
get all the exercise I could ever need.

160
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:38,100
I mean, do you see this view?

161
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,240
It's spectacular.

162
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,400
Wait, run that by me again.

163
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:43,197
You don't even have to leave?

164
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,557
Just how long have you been
living up there anyway?

165
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:48,517
I suppose I've been here
for about three years now.

166
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:49,430
What?

167
00:09:49,513 --> 00:09:50,343
Three years?

168
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:53,797
I probably haven't touched
terra firma in nearly a month.

169
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,586
What are we gonna do, Josuke?

170
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:59,880
I had no idea such an idiot was living
right under our noses in Morioh.

171
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,492
If you ask me, he's a pure great nutcase.

172
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:04,117
He's just living out a fantasy.

173
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,737
But there's no way he'd be
dumb enough to attack us.

174
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:07,660
You're right.

175
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:12,432
For now, at least, our best option is
heading back and reporting to Jotaro.

176
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:17,520
Then again, something just
doesn't feel right about this.

177
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,550
Hmm.

178
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:29,260
What is he doing there?

179
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:30,520
How strange.

180
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,777
I suppose children like to
take videos like anyone else.

181
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:36,213
But why is he hiding behind that pillar?

182
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:39,177
It's almost as if he's up
to the same thing I am.

183
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:42,600
He's following someone and
capturing their every move.

184
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,708
Could his target be
someone in this picture?

185
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:52,400
Hayato Kawajiri, huh?

186
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:57,420
There's something very
unusual about this kid.

187
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:11,740
Hey, I'm home! Huh?

188
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,493
Is that boy still here?

189
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,840
Hey, Josuke, it's time for school!

190
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:17,295
Haven't you left yet?

191
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:18,650
Josuke!

192
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:24,060
I could go for some food.

193
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,670
Hmm?

194
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,280
He did not.

195
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:32,757
That little shit only
thinks about himself.

196
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:35,557
He takes a giant bite out
of my favorite Comic-Core

197
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:39,228
custer and pops it back in the
fridge like it never happened?

198
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:40,857
And there were two in here.

199
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,234
Where's the other one?

200
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:45,615
Man, that kid pisses me off sometimes.

201
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:54,560
Hey, look sharp!

202
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,040
Something fell out of your pocket!

203
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,580
Hey, is that a photo?

204
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:04,477
Would you too mind skedaddling and -
Don't worry about picking that picture up.

205
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,457
I'll get it later.

206
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,837
It looks like an ordinary Polaroid to me.

207
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:11,080
Why is he so freaked out?
It's fine! Just leave!

208
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:16,257
What? You're...

209
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:19,440
Hey, what's going on, Josuke? That blast!

210
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,094
You're Kira's old man!

211
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:24,456
I should've known your crusty
ass was behind all this!

212
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,840
I've been waiting for this moment.

213
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,820
You've stepped into my abode.

214
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:34,437
If you tell someone to come in,
they chicken out and refuse,

215
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,997
but if you tell them the opposite,
they get pissed and enter!

216
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:41,060
You've at long last entered into
Superfly, Josuke Higashikata!

217
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,320
Wait, I've what?

218
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,880
Well done, Toyohiro Kanedaichi!

219
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:47,257
You lured him in, hook, line, and sinker!

220
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:49,516
Now our friend Josuke has a new home!

221
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,837
Gudos, my friend!

222
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,155
That sounds bad, bro!

223
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,297
You gotta come back!

224
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:55,060
Get moving, Josuke! No!

225
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,967
We finally found Kira's dad!

226
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,513
And he's got the arrow!

227
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,290
No!

228
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,640
Get back here!

229
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,908
I'm sure you're confused,
so let me explain.

230
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,037
Once someone steps into the tower's realm,

231
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:16,137
it won't spit them out until
its next victim steps in.

232
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:20,397
However, if they try to force their way
out, they simply become part of the tower.

233
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,715
That's the secret ability of my stand.

234
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:24,770
Superfly!

235
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:28,960
We've got you now, Josuke Higashikata!

236
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:32,940
Make sure he stays nice and
comfy now, Toyohiro! Ahahaha!

237
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:36,370
Kyousuke!

238
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:46,130
Kyousuke!

239
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,260
Damn it all!

240
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:53,277
I have a bit of a confession to make.

241
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:57,740
Superfly is indeed my stand, but
it isn't exactly under my control.

242
00:13:58,080 --> 00:14:00,277
It pretty much does whatever it wants.

243
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:03,040
And now that you're here, I can take off.

244
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,220
I've been trapped by Superfly
for the entirety of my stay here.

245
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:09,980
Well, take care of her for me.

246
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,591
I've got a life to enjoy.

247
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,550
So,

248
00:14:13,633 --> 00:14:17,437
the sly son of a bitch is in cahoots with
that grandpa ghost dude from the picture.

249
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:18,350
Mr.

250
00:14:18,433 --> 00:14:21,077
